    "created_at": "2017-07-04T11:25:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-04T11:25:37Z",
    "body": "> an element that accepts content other than phrasing content as well as phrasing content\r\n\r\nThe `<p>` element does not accept `non-phrasing` content, thus it's not one of the elements specified above. Does this mean a run of phrasing content within  `<p>` won't form a paragraph?\r\n\r\nIn my opinion, the statement \"in an element that accepts non-xxx as well as xxx\" is not useful. The current spec may be better expressed as:\r\n\r\n> Then, in view, for each run of sibling phrasing content nodes uninterrupted by other types of content, in an element that accepts phrasing content, let first be the first node of the run, and let last be the last node of the run.\r\n\r\n@domenic How do you think?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
